  "content": {
    "id": "p75-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": {
      "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
      "version": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "p75-q6-title",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "[A root that doesn’t move]",
              "marks": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p75-q6-introduction",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "For an integer ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "n\\ne 2",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", consider",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p75-q6-equation",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "center",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "y=(n-2)x^2+4x-(n+2).",
              "display": true
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p75-q6-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that its discriminant is $4n^2$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\Delta=4n^2$.",
          "worked": "Here $a=n-2$, $b=4$ and $c=-(n+2)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=4^2-4(n-2)(-(n+2))\\\\\\Delta&=16+4(n^2-4)\\\\\\Delta&=4n^2.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p75-q6-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Factorise the quadratic. (Hint: split the middle term)",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x-1)((n-2)x+n+2)$.",
          "worked": "Split the middle term using $4x=-(n-2)x+(n+2)x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=(n-2)x^2-(n-2)x+(n+2)x-(n+2)\\\\y&=(n-2)x(x-1)+(n+2)(x-1)\\\\y&=(x-1)((n-2)x+n+2).\\end{align*}$$\nExpanding confirms the original quadratic:\n$$\\begin{align*}(x-1)((n-2)x+n+2)&=(n-2)x^2+((n+2)-(n-2))x-(n+2)\\\\&=(n-2)x^2+4x-(n+2).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      },
      {
        "id": "p75-q6-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Hence show that one $x$-intercept is the same for every permitted value of $n$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=1$ for every permitted value of $n$.",
          "worked": "The factor $x-1$ is present for every permitted value of $n$. Setting $x-1=0$ gives $x=1$, so the fixed $x$-intercept is $(1,0)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p75-q6-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Find the other $x$-intercept in terms of $n$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-\\dfrac{n+2}{n-2}$.",
          "worked": "The second factor gives\n$$\\begin{align*}(n-2)x+n+2&=0\\\\(n-2)x&=-(n+2)\\\\x&=-\\frac{n+2}{n-2}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p75-q6-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "Explain why all the roots are rational.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "One root is $1$; the other is a ratio of integers with a non-zero denominator.",
          "worked": "The first root is the integer $1$. The second is $-\\dfrac{n+2}{n-2}$, a ratio of integers because $n$ is an integer. Since $n\\ne2$, its denominator is non-zero. Both roots are rational.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 22
      },
      {
        "id": "p75-q6-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "For which value of $n$ is the parabola tangent to the $x$-axis?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$n=0$.",
          "worked": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p75-q6-f-tangency-reason",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Tangency occurs when the discriminant is zero.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p75-q6-f-tangency-working",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\begin{aligned}4n^2&=0\\\\n&=0.\\end{aligned}",
                    "display": true
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p75-q6-f-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Therefore, the quadratic becomes ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "y=-2(x-1)^2",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", tangent to the ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "x",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "-axis at ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "(1,0)",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
